DMCOMMANDS - Your staff and DM powers

Syntax: dmcommands
        dmcommands native [page]
Alias: dmhelp
Also: help dm, help staff

The default guide lists HollowDeep tools based on your saved staff role and
builder assignments. The native index lists original * commands allowed by
your native caretaker/DM class. Command-specific target and room rules remain.
The guide does not grant powers, change class or perform any listed action.

Mod and Implementor are separate roles with equal authority. Admins and
Owners have additional tools. Builder assignments are independent of roles.
An Owner with an ordinary playable class does not acquire native * commands.
The named-operator-only *flushrooms command stays unavailable while its
configured operator name is empty. See help hstaff, help hbuild and help hdm.
